  ],
  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {目|め}を{逸|そ}らす: to avert one's eyes\n- {視線|しせん}を{逸|そ}らす: to look away\n- {話題|わだい}を{逸|そ}らす: to change the subject\n- {注意|ちゅうい}を{逸|そ}らす: to divert attention\n\nUSAGE: Always takes an object (what is being turned away). The most common pattern is {目|め}を{逸|そ}らす. Can imply avoidance or discomfort.",
